From 4301c2d306b6cbb08e6f07e49ae30fe8b0f1c09a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaul Lavochkin <shaul9191@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:58:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] wasm: record await spans for run-time AsyncLocalStorage
 hooks

A scoped parser collector records each `await` expression's keyword start
and operand end, and each `for await` loop's start (its outermost label)
and body span, using the end of the previous token the lexer now keeps.
With BUNWASM_AWAIT_HOOKS on, the printer passes a direct eval's argument
through `__bunwasm_evalSource`, so the browser engine can splice its
AsyncLocalStorage hooks into source compiled at run time while the call
stays a direct eval.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
